  "statement": "Return the length of the longest path between any two nodes, measured in edges. The path does not have to pass through the root.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= node count <= 10^4"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "For any node, the longest path THROUGH it is leftHeight + rightHeight edges.",
    "So compute heights recursively, and while doing so track the best value of that sum anywhere.",
    "The answer is that running maximum, not the return value of the recursion. Those are two different quantities."
  ],
